🧑 User types in the search bar → submits form

🌐 Browser sends GET request → /listings?q=beach

🧩 Server reads req.query.q

💾 MongoDB finds matching titles using regex

🎨 EJS renders the matching results

$regex stands for Regular Expression.

It lets MongoDB search for partial text matches — not just exact matches.

The "i" means case-insensitive search (ignore uppercase/lowercase).

Without "i", MongoDB will only match exact case.    